{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createCursorPager<T>(__namedParameters): CursorPager<T>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/query-db-collection/src/cursor-pagination.ts#L50","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-db-collection/src/cursor-pagination.ts:50"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fulfill offset/limit windows using opaque backend cursors. Query owns the\npages, freshness, invalidation and garbage collection. Use one dedicated key\nper filtered, totally ordered source. Loading more reuses fresh pages; refreshing\nstale data rebuilds the loaded sequence from its first page."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key must not also be used for ordinary QueryCollection row arrays.\nUse sibling row/page prefixes under one resource prefix, not pages beneath\nthe row prefix (manual writes update that whole prefix). For a forced refresh,\ncancel the resource prefix before invalidating it. A positive staleTime avoids\nrefreshing on every read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reads on one pager serialize; separate pagers share Query's cache and fetches.\nAborting a reader discards its answer, not shared cached\npages. Cancel the query through QueryClient to cancel its transport. Neither\ncancellation nor a TTL can repair a backend's inconsistent cursor sequence."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"namedparameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"__namedParameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/CursorPagerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CursorPagerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/CursorPager.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CursorPager"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"namedparameters","text":"__namedParameters","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createCursorPager<T>(__namedParameters): CursorPager<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-db-collection/src/cursor-pagination.ts:50](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/query-db-collection/src/cursor-pagination.ts#L50)\n\nFulfill offset/limit windows using opaque backend cursors. Query owns the\npages, freshness, invalidation and garbage collection. Use one dedicated key\nper filtered, totally ordered source. Loading more reuses fresh pages; refreshing\nstale data rebuilds the loaded sequence from its first page.\n\nThe key must not also be used for ordinary QueryCollection row arrays.\nUse sibling row/page prefixes under one resource prefix, not pages beneath\nthe row prefix (manual writes update that whole prefix). For a forced refresh,\ncancel the resource prefix before invalidating it. A positive staleTime avoids\nrefreshing on every read.\n\nReads on one pager serialize; separate pagers share Query's cache and fetches.\nAborting a reader discards its answer, not shared cached\npages. Cancel the query through QueryClient to cancel its transport. Neither\ncancellation nor a TTL can repair a backend's inconsistent cursor sequence.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### \\_\\_namedParameters\n\n[`CursorPagerOptions`](../interfaces/CursorPagerOptions.md)\\<`T`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CursorPager`](../interfaces/CursorPager.md)\\<`T`\\>\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createCursorPager\ntitle: createCursorPager\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createCursorPager<T>(__namedParameters): CursorPager<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-db-collection/src/cursor-pagination.ts:50](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/query-db-collection/src/cursor-pagination.ts#L50)\n\nFulfill offset/limit windows using opaque backend cursors. Query owns the\npages, freshness, invalidation and garbage collection. Use one dedicated key\nper filtered, totally ordered source. Loading more reuses fresh pages; refreshing\nstale data rebuilds the loaded sequence from its first page.\n\nThe key must not also be used for ordinary QueryCollection row arrays.\nUse sibling row/page prefixes under one resource prefix, not pages beneath\nthe row prefix (manual writes update that whole prefix). For a forced refresh,\ncancel the resource prefix before invalidating it. A positive staleTime avoids\nrefreshing on every read.\n\nReads on one pager serialize; separate pagers share Query's cache and fetches.\nAborting a reader discards its answer, not shared cached\npages. Cancel the query through QueryClient to cancel its transport. Neither\ncancellation nor a TTL can repair a backend's inconsistent cursor sequence.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### \\_\\_namedParameters\n\n[`CursorPagerOptions`](../interfaces/CursorPagerOptions.md)\\<`T`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CursorPager`](../interfaces/CursorPager.md)\\<`T`\\>\n"}
